{"id": "EUVD-2026-76682", "enisaUuid": "82e55d23-bb7c-3b8b-b328-66e1cf46bf75", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niomap: don't free integrity payload that doesn't exist\n\nfs_bio_integrity_alloc might not allocate a bio integrity payload if PI\nverification is disabled on the block device.  Check for that case before\ncalling fs_bio_integrity_free in iomap_bio_read_folio_range_sync to\navoid a NULL pointer dereferences.\n\nMake the branch cover the PI verification as well - while\nfs_bio_integrity_verify works without an integrity payload, it requires\none to actually do useful work.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:47:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65651f1001aa3638909bc58c7b2b46160692757b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a8685b32c0718cc7b2cb4d6202e5a5b8e0a8e2d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p8q7-qqp3-r9v3", "CVE-2026-89770"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c7e9c66-22ca-3e11-8341-e6d07cab67c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b10a370529cbd7b918c1eef43d409e43d9e0b78 <8a8685b32c0718cc7b2cb4d6202e5a5b8e0a8e2d"}, {"id": "1451b180-3847-3644-b7ae-05c2ce77a787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "aa6a1dd6-481a-3b39-98e6-2a70ec1d1abb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ae6994c7-fbd8-3ad4-b135-0ecc7d08e3f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "e68610ca-eb8b-357b-bec9-346b188f80bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b10a370529cbd7b918c1eef43d409e43d9e0b78 <65651f1001aa3638909bc58c7b2b46160692757b"}, {"id": "f97f5038-06dc-372d-94dc-2bfe928db50e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisa